The widths are held as a table of numbers; those of a few characters that the two fonts do not have (a pi, a
prime, an arrow, subscript digits) were added.

Residue templates (src/bindview/residues.py) follow the wwPDB Chemical Component Dictionary, which is in the
public domain (CC0 1.0).

In the repository, not in the package
-------------------------------------

Structures under testdata/ are entries of the RCSB Protein Data Bank, whose data are in the public domain
(CC0 1.0); each folder's meta.json names its entry. Berman et al., Nucleic Acids Res. 2000, 28, 235.

testdata/interface_pae: models and predicted aligned errors of the AlphaFold Protein Structure Database
(CC BY 4.0; Jumper et al., Nature 2021, 596, 583; Varadi et al., Nucleic Acids Res. 2024, 52, D368). The files
are the database's, packed. The domain borders are from The Encyclopedia of Domains (CC BY 4.0).

scripts/solvent_validation_set.tsv lists the Astex Diverse Set (Hartshorn et al., J. Med. Chem. 2007, 50, 726)
with the ligand of each entry as PoseBusters names it (Buttenschoen et al., Chem. Sci. 2024, 15, 3130).

testdata/nucleic/riboswitch_bisguanidine and testdata/md/riboswitch_bisguanidine: a frame and contact tables of
the molecular dynamics simulations of a guanidine-II riboswitch with a bivalent ligand by the author of bindview
(Steuer et al., NAR Genom. Bioinform. 2024, 6, lqae132; https://doi.org/10.1093/nargab/lqae132), taken from
https://github.com/jakob-steuer/FHNW-Summer-School-2025-MolSim-Analysis (MIT).

testdata/ensemble_bioemu2: samples of BioEmu 2 (Microsoft), whose code and checkpoint are under the MIT licence.

testdata/*/interactions.tsv were written by PLIP (Adasme et al., Nucleic Acids Res. 2021, 49, W530), which is
GPL-2.0 and not part of this repository.
